# Portal design system

## shadcn first (mandatory)

- Prefer components from `components/ui/*` (shadcn). Do not invent one-off UI primitives.
- If a custom component is needed, compose it from existing shadcn pieces (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `Field`, `Dialog`, etc.) plus tokens — never raw HTML controls or parallel design systems.
- Add new shadcn UI via the project’s shadcn workflow into `components/ui/`; do not copy paste third-party component libs.

## Buttons

- Primary actions (submit, save, continue, CTA): always `size="lg"`.
- Prefer `variant="default"` for primary; use `outline` / `secondary` / `ghost` only when matching an existing pattern.
- Do not use ad-hoc button classes that bypass `Button` / `buttonVariants`.

```tsx
// ✅
<Button type="submit" size="lg">Submit</Button>

// ❌
<button className="px-4 py-2 bg-red-500">Submit</button>
<Button size="default">Submit</Button> // primary CTA
```

## Visual consistency (whole portal)

- **Colors**: only CSS variables from `globals.css` (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, etc.). No hard-coded hex/rgb/oklch in components unless matching an established layout token already used in that screen.
- **Fonts**: use theme fonts (`font-sans` / heading tokens). Do not introduce new font families per page.
- **Type scale**: reuse the same sizes as nearby screens (e.g. auth titles `text-2xl font-bold`, body/labels via Field + default Input). Do not invent one-off `text-[13px]` / random weights per page.
- **Spacing / radius**: use Tailwind spacing and theme radius (`rounded-lg`, etc.) consistently with existing pages.
- Every new page must feel like the same product: same tokens, same control sizes, same hierarchy.

## Strictness

- Match existing page patterns before inventing new layouts.
- If unsure, copy structure from the closest similar screen (auth, dashboard, settings) and only swap content.
- Design deviations need an explicit user request — do not “improve” colors, fonts, or button sizes unilaterally.
